.TH "PB-CONFIG-CUSTOMIZE-EXPLAIN" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-customize-explain - Show command expansion without executing it


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config customize explain -- <arguments...> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show command expansion without executing it

.PP
Expand the supplied command arguments using the current local shortcuts and defaults without running the result. Place arguments after -- so they are interpreted as the proposed command.

.PP
Customization is local to this CLI installation. It can change shortcuts, command defaults, and terminal appearance without changing account credentials or remote resources. Validate or explain preferences before applying an unfamiliar document.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for explain

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config-customize(1)\fP
